{"ld": 1943, "paper": "HP1302", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Establish a Commission to Study the Role of Private Equity in Maine's Economy and in Key Economic Sectors", "sponsor_id": "h-pugh-dylan", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bennett-richard", "s-grohoski-nicole", "h-rana-ambureen", "h-sato-eleanor", "h-sayre-daniel", "s-talbot-ross-rachel"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This resolve establishes the Commission to Study Private Equity Firms to conduct a comprehensive study of the role of private equity firms in the State's economy, with a focus on transparency, investment practices and private equity's effects on key sectors such as energy, health care, housing and nursing homes. The commission must issue a report with its findings and recommendations to the Joint Standing Committee on Health Coverage, Insurance and Financial Services no later than December 3, 2025, which may include legislative proposals to address the effects of private equity firms on the State's economy and on key economic sectors, such as energy, health care, housing and nursing homes.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1302&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1943)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1302&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-739)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1302&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-739)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Senate", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1302&item=2&snum=132",